-- Reverse 0063. Purely additive forward, so purely subtractive back:
-- drop what was added and nothing else.
--
-- Note what this does NOT have to do. The earlier draft renamed
-- `senders.replied_count` and dropped `sender_timeseries.reply_count`,
-- so its rollback had to RECONSTRUCT both by re-running the old
-- thread-membership aggregate — correct, verified, and still a
-- computation standing between a bad deploy and a working database.
-- Leaving the old columns in place removes that step entirely: the
-- values were never touched, so there is nothing to rebuild.
DROP INDEX IF EXISTS "senders_account_normalized_email_idx";
